1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:05,310
In this video, we'll install PadDeck on your PC and on your tablet.

2
00:00:06,010 --> 00:00:09,979
First, open the PadDeck Releases page on GitHub,

3
00:00:09,979 --> 00:00:14,858
and download two files: the PadDeck setup file for Windows,

4
00:00:14,858 --> 00:00:17,670
and PadDeck dot A P K for Android.

5
00:00:18,370 --> 00:00:21,293
On your PC, double-click the setup file.

6
00:00:21,293 --> 00:00:26,993
If Windows shows a blue box saying Windows protected your PC, click More info,

7
00:00:26,993 --> 00:00:28,162
then Run anyway.

8
00:00:28,162 --> 00:00:32,255
It appears because the installer isn't digitally signed.

9
00:00:32,255 --> 00:00:34,520
Then click Install, and Finish.

10
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:40,031
PadDeck opens, and a blue PadDeck icon appears in the system tray,

11
00:00:40,031 --> 00:00:42,656
at the bottom right of your taskbar.

12
00:00:42,656 --> 00:00:47,030
If Windows Firewall asks, allow PadDeck on private networks.

13
00:00:47,730 --> 00:00:50,495
Now let's install the app on your tablet.

14
00:00:50,495 --> 00:00:54,002
In PadDeck on your PC, click Devices in the sidebar,

15
00:00:54,002 --> 00:00:56,970
and find the box called Get the Android app.

16
00:00:57,670 --> 00:01:02,586
Scan that code with your tablet's camera, and open the downloaded file.

17
00:01:02,586 --> 00:01:08,540
When Android asks, allow installing apps from this source, then tap Install, and Open.

